{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And YHWH said to her.</b> Through an agent; it was said to her in the Holy Spirit, and He said it to her (Bereshit Rabbah)." "<b>Two nations in your womb.</b> גיים is written; these are Antoninus and Rabbi, from whose table never ceased either radish or lettuce, neither in the days of the sun nor in the days of the rains (Avodah Zarah 11)." "<b>And two peoples.</b> לְאֹם means nothing but kingdom." "<b>From your womb they shall separate.</b> From the womb they separate, this one to his wickedness and this one to his innocence." "<b>The one shall be filled from the other.</b> They will not be equal in greatness — when this one rises, that one falls. And so it says: ״אֶתְמַלֵּא הַחֳרָבָה״ (Ezekiel 26) — Tyre was not filled except from the destruction of Jerusalem."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {1 "Rashi reads the word גוים as written גיים (geyim, 'great ones'), referring to the famous friendship between the Roman emperor Antoninus and Rabbi Yehudah HaNasi."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:00:29.209986966Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}